=== WHAT WAS BUILT (parity with the web source, read end-to-end) ===
  ClimateSection is the Climate section of the Vehicle Detail page: a GlassPanel with a
  Wind-icon "Climate" header over either an eight-tile MetricCard grid (when a climate
  snapshot is present) or an EmptyState ("No climate data available"). The native surface
  reproduces its data, composition, every state, and i18n keys via shared P1/S8
  state-holder seams (no view I/O):

  Composition (web → native), all EIGHT MetricCards reproduced VERBATIM (not stubbed):
   1. Inside Temp      — formatTemperature(inside_temp ?? inside_temp_c), thermometer glyph,
                         green accent chip.
   2. Outside Temp     — formatTemperature(outside_temp ?? outside_temp_c), thermometer,
                         cyan accent chip.
   3. Driver Setpoint  — formatTemperature(driver_temp_setting ?? driver_setpoint_c),
                         thermometer, purple accent chip.
   4. Fan Speed        — hvac_fan_status ?? fan_status (raw integer, web String(n)), else
                         em-dash; wind glyph, cyan.
   5. Seat Heater Left — "Level {seat_heater_left}" else em-dash; CircleDot glyph, green.
   6. Seat Heater Right— "Level {seat_heater_right}" else em-dash; CircleDot, green.
   7. Defrost          — raw defrost_mode verbatim when active (mode present and != "Off"),
                         else localized "Off"; snowflake glyph, green when active else cyan.
   8. Climate On       — (is_ac_on ?? is_climate_on) ? "On" : "Off"; flame glyph, green when
                         on else cyan.

  Temperature pipeline ported VERBATIM from lib/unitConversion.ts: formatTemperature →
  convertTempFromSI (°C identity / °F = c*9/5+32) + formatNumber (grouped, locale-aware,
  half-up; DEFAULT_PRECISION.temperature = 1; °unit appended with NO space; nullish /
  non-finite → emptyDisplay "—"). SI °C is read directly from the seam; conversion happens
  only at the render boundary (web useUnits), honouring the frontend SI cutover.

  Note (legacy-alias fidelity): the web coalesces each pre-migration alias over its SI
  canonical column (inside_temp ?? inside_temp_c, …, is_ac_on ?? is_climate_on). Modelled
  as both fields on ClimateSectionReading with `resolved*` accessors reproducing `?? `
  verbatim (the legacy alias is preferred when present), unit tested.

  Accent fidelity (ADR-006 semantic, not literal): the web MetricCard `color` prop tints
  ONLY the icon chip (bg/ring/glyph), not the value. green → statusSuccess, cyan →
  statusInfo, purple → chartSeriesPower; the defrost / climate-on tiles flip green↔cyan by
  state. The value reads textPrimary; the label reads textSecondary.

